DeepPixBiS architecture reference:
Anjith George and Sebastien Marcel, "Deep Pixel-wise Binary Supervision for
Face Presentation Attack Detection," ICB 2019.

The Specialist architecture follows the publicly described architecture and
the feature slice/pixel/global computation in Idiap's bob.pad.face:
https://github.com/bioidiap/bob.pad.face/blob/555f181a76fa39d20f0c61ef1dc616bd85b817c1/src/bob/pad/face/deep_pix_bis.py

The new specialist implementation is distributed under GPL-3.0-only; the
accompanying COPYING contains the license. The surrounding experimental
controller uses this module. No upstream PAD checkpoint or Bob training
pipeline is bundled. This is a fixed matched-input retraining recipe,
not reproduction of the original paper's training results.

Torchvision and PyTorch retain their respective licenses. ImageNet DenseNet
initialization is a separately acquired torchvision artifact after explicit
owner approval; it is not redistributed in this repository.
